.TH LINK-HOARDER 1 "" "link-hoarder 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
link-hoarder \- manage bookmarks and import browser data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B link-hoarder
.RI [ --backend " local|api" ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Link Hoarder stores bookmarks in local SQLite or through an HTTP API. Commands return bookmark data as JSON. Bookmark URLs can use HTTP, HTTPS, or javascript: schemes. Link Hoarder stores bookmarklets but does not execute them.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create URL --title TITLE
Create a bookmark. Use --folder and repeated --tag options for metadata.
.TP
.B list [--query TEXT] [--limit NUMBER] [--offset NUMBER]
List bookmarks. Filter titles and URLs with --query.
.TP
.B get ID
Get one bookmark.
.TP
.B update ID [--url URL] [--title TITLE] [--folder FOLDER] [--tag TAG]
Update supplied bookmark fields.
.TP
.B delete ID
Delete one bookmark.
.TP
.B import-browser BROWSER [--profile FILE]
Import chrome, chromium, edge, or firefox profile data. Omit --profile to discover profiles.
.TP
.B import-file FILE
Import a Netscape bookmark HTML export.
.TP
.B config
Show saved backend configuration without secrets.
.TP
.B api [--host HOST] [--port PORT]
Run the FastAPI server. Set LINK_HOARDER_API_KEY first.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_BACKEND
CLI backend. Use local or api.
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_API_URL
API server root URL. Do not include /api/v1.
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_API_KEY
API key used by API clients and the server.
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_API_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
CLI HTTP timeout in seconds. The default is 10.
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_DATABASE_PATH
SQLite database path. The default uses the platform-native user data directory.
.TP
.B LINK_HOARDER_LOG_LEVEL
Structured log level. The default is INFO.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I docs/readthedocs/reference/configuration.md
Complete configuration reference.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates a missing bookmark. Two indicates invalid backend or server configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uvx (1),
.BR docker-compose (1)
